//FIRST GET THE SOURCE CODE FROM GIT SO YOU CAN GET APP.PY AND REQUIREMENTS.TXT AND RELATED FILES IN YOUR SERVER. AND INSTALL PYTHON-PIP MANUALLY IN YOUR SERVER TO GET DEPENDENCIES from THE REQUIREMENT.TXT FLILE
//INITIALLY PYTHON IS INSTALLED IN YOUR EC2 INSTANCE, INSTALL ONLY PIP

CLONE THE GIT URL USING:>>>>>>> git clone url
NOW WE HAVE THE PYTHON CODE

COMMAND TO INSTALL PIP:>>>>>>>>> yum install python-pip -y
NOW INSTALL DEPENDECIES FROM REQ.TXT:>>>>>>> pip install -r requirments.txt
=====================================================================================================================================================

DOCKER-FILE:

FROM python
WORKDIR /myapp
COPY req.txt .
RUN pip install -r req.txt
COPY . .  //GETTING APP.PY AND OTHER REQUIRED FILES
CMD ["python","app.py"]

NOW BUILD THIS DOCKER IMAGE. 
---------> docker build -t python-image:v1
TO CHECK IMAGE USE:>>>>> docker images

NOW RUN THE IMAGE TO CREATE THE CONTAINER
---------> docker ru -itd --name python-cont -p 1122:8000 python-image:v1
TO CHECK THE CREATED CONTAINER IS RUNNING OR NOT USE:>>>> doocker ps

NOW ACCESS THE APPLICATION WITH YOUR IP WITH HOST PORT 1122.
